+You are a senior desktop UI/UX engineer specializing in modern Tkinter applications.
+
+Refactor my existing Tkinter/ttk application UI without changing any business logic, calculations, data models, event handling, or program behavior.
+
+Goals:
+- Make the application look like a modern engineering/industrial desktop tool.
+- Keep using Tkinter and ttk only.
+- Do NOT migrate to PyQt, Qt, Kivy, Electron, or web technologies.
+- Preserve all existing functionality.
+
+Design requirements:
+
+1. Visual hierarchy
+- Replace excessive LabelFrames with cleaner ttk.Frame containers.
+- Use whitespace, padding, and section headers instead of many bordered boxes.
+- Make primary areas visually distinct using spacing rather than heavy borders.
+
+2. Layout
+- Reorganize the interface into three main sections:
+  - Left sidebar: input data and format management.
+  - Main area: best solutions table.
+  - Bottom details area: selected solution details.
+
+Suggested structure:
+
+--------------------------------------------------------------
+| Toolbar                                           | Calcola |
+--------------------------------------------------------------
+| Sidebar         | Best Solutions                            |
+|                 |                                           |
+| Dati MT         | Treeview                                  |
+| Formati         |                                           |
+|                 |                                           |
+|                 |-------------------------------------------|
+|                 | Selected Solution Details                 |
+|                 |                                           |
+|                 | Tabs: Panoramica | Cassetti | Teste Robot |
+|                 |-------------------------------------------|
+
+
+4. Typography
+- Use Segoe UI.
+- Section titles should use:
+    Segoe UI Semibold 11 or 12.
+- Normal text:
+    Segoe UI 10.
+
+5. Spacing
+- Add consistent internal padding:
+    10-15 px around major sections.
+- Add vertical spacing between logical groups.
+
+6. Main action button
+- Make "Calcola" the primary action.
+- Increase its size.
+- Place it prominently in the top toolbar.
+- Use ttk styling to make it stand out.
+
+7. Tabs
+- Replace the simultaneous display of:
+    - Panoramica formati
+    - Tipi di cassetti utilizzati
+    - Tipi di teste robot utilizzate
+  with a ttk.Notebook.
+
+10. Styling
+- Create a centralized ttk.Style configuration.
+- Use a modern light theme.
+- Avoid the classic Windows 95/XP appearance.
+- Keep the UI professional and suitable for manufacturing/engineering software.
+
+Implementation requirements:
+- Return complete modified code.
+- Explain every layout change.
+- Do not remove any existing widgets.
+- Do not alter functionality.
+- Preserve all variable names and callbacks whenever possible.
+- Refactor only the presentation layer.

